# /etc/mosquitto/beacon.passwd — SHAPE ONLY. Never commit a real one.
# Create it on hub with mosquitto_passwd, which prompts for each password
# and writes a salted hash (mosquitto 2.x uses $7$ PBKDF2-SHA512):
#
#   sudo mosquitto_passwd -c /etc/mosquitto/beacon.passwd beacon-svc   # -c creates the file
#   sudo mosquitto_passwd    /etc/mosquitto/beacon.passwd beacon-dev   # no -c: append
#   sudo chown root:mosquitto /etc/mosquitto/beacon.passwd && sudo chmod 640 /etc/mosquitto/beacon.passwd
#
# beacon-svc's password goes into ~/.config/beacon/config.toml [mqtt] password.
# beacon-dev's password goes into the device provisioning (chunk 3) and
# tools/watch.py on workstation.
#
# The resulting file looks like (hashes here are fake):
beacon-svc:$7$101$FAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKE==
beacon-dev:$7$101$FAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKEFAKE==
